<description>&lt;p&gt;Intercommunal clashes in Rumbek have killed dozens of civilians, prompting caretaker governor Rin Tueny to return to Lakes State, while a curfew was imposed to curb the violence. Two SSPDF soldiers were wounded in an attack on a Mundri West military outpost, and the U.S. Embassy condemned an assault on WFP workers in Jonglei that involved looting of aid. A Juba High Court sentenced five officers to 24 years for a raid on a general's home, and Pibor appealed to Jonglei authorities to return 81 abducted women and children. The lethal communal violence now far exceeds the two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiREFVX3lxTFBZV2l2WWEwN0hJeEVwNkVsaE9iVGFJZDY2VnAxQXRWbEI3Z0pzWWJnV195My0tbTZUN0ZtWE9FYnhaQXJi0gFKQVVfeXFMTmxyN0hCbzdqSGpsblBxa2pSYTljOXhpTlkzNE95aGQzZGpoU3dBc2U5VnJBSlYtTEZvd1dGbWlsbDlIOEJ3OUh3UkE?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxNajRneUIzNVQwRGtLeEtpSm9jOThWdFNWOEJqb0JaamxPQ2xtVUdWTExXQzZwbVllZ1c2UDhSWlg3Z2JxQlJ6blhrVXR3OEdPbzBvZTZWdXlZWmxFZEl0X3A4MVFqbEtTTlFnOG5XaWtWSUR2Rm5ibzNuQ0YwbGJBdU03SWFZdEhobHRKbGFxN3NnQ0cyWklxYkxiMkFiRUc1bllUcmV2S1diWGs?oc=5&quot;&gt;The New Humanitarian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMitgFBVV95cUxQbFdiNnNBUVRGTlN1X0tab0hKQUxZOUxLVk5Fb19RTGVMQkx2TkM2VkU0eFItYUhiNnlUSzRnZmc4dHdHZ1ZhVGlyM3dNTmIycEJ2RjZoYi0zRkFiUmFfczRETXpBMWFNQlBUZEFyal9ybGpiMTV